  ○ [p2_backend] Build FastAPI backend with SQLite
    agent:  Backend Developer (programmer_1)
    desc:   Create the complete backend for the note app at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_002/backend/

1. Create requirements.txt with: fastapi, uvicorn, sqlalchemy, python-multipart, pydantic
2. Create main.py with FastAPI app containing:
   - SQLite database via SQLAlchemy (notes table: id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, title TEXT, content TEXT, created_at TIMESTAMP, updated_at TIMESTAMP)
   - CORS middleware (allow all origins for dev)
   - GET /notes - list all notes
   - POST /notes - create note (title, content)
   - GET /notes/{id} - get single note
   - PUT /notes/{id} - update note
   - DELETE /notes/{id} - delete note
   - Models: NoteCreate (title: str, content: str), NoteUpdate (title: Optional[str], content: Optional[str])
3. Create a models.py file for SQLAlchemy models
4. Create schemas.py for Pydantic schemas
5. Create database.py for DB connection
6. Set up venv in the backend directory (python3 -m venv venv)
7. Make sure all imports work and the app can start with: uvicorn main:app --reload

Note: After creating venv, activate and install requirements. The backend should be fully functional.
  ○ [p3_frontend] Build Next.js frontend with BlockNote
    agent:  Frontend Developer (programmer_2)
    desc:   Create the complete frontend at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_002/frontend/

1. Initialize Next.js project with App Router:
   npx create-next-app@latest frontend --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app --src-dir --no-import-alias --use-npm
   This must be run INSIDE /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_002/ (cd to parent dir first)

2. Install dependencies:
   npm install @blocknote/react @blocknote/core @shadcn/ui lucide-react
   Also: npx shadcn@latest init -d (for shadcn init with defaults)
   Add shadcn components: npx shadcn@latest add button card input -y

3. Create app structure:
   src/app/page.tsx - Main page with sidebar + editor layout
   src/app/layout.tsx - Root layout
   src/components/Sidebar.tsx - Note list sidebar component
   src/components/NoteEditor.tsx - BlockNote editor component
   src/components/NoteViewer.tsx - BlockNote viewer/rendering component

4. Key features:
   - Sidebar fetches notes from GET http://localhost:8000/notes
   - Click note in sidebar → load it in editor
   - '+' button in sidebar → create new note
   - Delete button on each note in sidebar
   - Editor auto-saves on content change (debounced, PUT to backend)
   - BlockNote @blocknote/react with @blocknote/core
   - Use the Theme from shadcn (dark/light)
   - API calls to http://localhost:8000

5. Create src/lib/api.ts with helper functions for all CRUD operations using fetch

Make sure all components compile and the app can start with 'npm run dev'.
